361	</head>
362	<body>
363		<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
364		<header id="top">
365			<h1>Welcome</h1>
366			<nav aria-label="Page sections">
367				<ul>
368					<li><a href="#features">Features</a></li>
369					<li><a href="#examples">Examples</a></li>
370					<li><a href="#resources">Resources</a></li>
371				</ul>
372			</nav>
373		</header>
374		<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
375			<section aria-label="Introduction">
376				<p>This is a well-structured, accessible HTML5 document demonstrating modern best practices for semantic markup and inclusive design.</p>
377				<p>
378					It uses semantic landmarks, a skip link for keyboard navigation,
379					and CSS that adapts to your light or dark mode preference.
380				</p>
381				<p>
382					Text and link colors meet WCAG AA contrast in both themes, type scales
383					with your browser's font size, and motion respects your system settings.
384				</p>
385			</section>
386	
387			<section aria-labelledby="features">
388				<h2 id="features">Features</h2>
389				<ul>
390					<li>Semantic HTML structure with proper landmarks</li>
391					<li>Keyboard accessible navigation and focus management</li>
392					<li>Dark mode support with custom color schemes</li>
393					<li>Responsive typography using modern CSS</li>
394					<li>Print-friendly styles for better readability</li>
395					<li>WCAG AA contrast compliance in all color modes</li>
396				</ul>
397			</section>
398	
399			<section aria-labelledby="examples">
400				<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>
401				<article class="card">
402					<h3>Component Cards</h3>
403					<p>Card components are useful for organizing related content. They include a subtle border and padding for visual separation.</p>
404					<a class="button" href="#resources">Learn more<span class="visually-hidden"> about accessibility resources</span></a>
405				</article>
406	
407				<article class="card">
408					<h3>Interactive Elements</h3>
409					<p>Buttons and links are fully accessible with clear focus states. All interactive elements include visible focus indicators and proper ARIA labels.</p>
410					<p><strong>Keyboard navigation:</strong> Use <kbd>Tab</kbd> to move forward, <kbd>Shift+Tab</kbd> to move backward, and <kbd>Enter</kbd> to activate.</p>
411				</article>
412	
413				<article class="card">
414					<h3>Accessible Form</h3>
415					<form id="contact-form">
416						<p class="form-hint">Fields marked <span aria-hidden="true">*</span> are required.</p>
417						<div class="field">
418							<label for="email">Email <span aria-hidden="true">*</span><span class="visually-hidden"> (required)</span></label>
419							<input type="email" id="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required aria-describedby="email-help">
420							<small id="email-help" class="form-hint">Please enter a valid email address</small>
421						</div>
422						<div class="field">
423							<label for="message">Message</label>
424							<textarea id="message" name="message" rows="4"></textarea>
425						</div>
426						<button type="submit">Send message</button>
427						<p id="form-status" role="status"></p>
428					</form>
429				</article>
430	
431				<article class="card">
432					<h3>Live Region Example</h3>
433					<p>Click the button to announce a message using a live region. This demonstrates how screen readers are notified of dynamic updates.</p>
434					<button id="announce" type="button">Announce message</button>
435					<div class="live-region" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
436						<span id="live-message"></span>
437					</div>
438				</article>
439			</section>
440	
441			<section aria-labelledby="resources">
442				<h2 id="resources">Resources</h2>
443				<p>Want to learn more about web accessibility and semantic HTML? Check out these resources:</p>
444				<ul>
445					<li><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/quickref/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WCAG 2.2 Quick Reference<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span></a></li>
446					<li><a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HTML Living Standard<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span></a></li>
447					<li><a href="https://www.a11y-101.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">A11y 101<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span></a></li>
448				</ul>
449			</section>
450		</main>
451		<footer>
452			<nav aria-label="Footer links">
453				<ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
454					<li><a href="#top">Back to top</a></li>
455					<li><a href="https://github.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span></a></li>
456				</ul>
457			</nav>
458			<p><small>&copy; <time datetime="2026">2026</time>. All rights reserved.</small></p>
459		</footer>
460		<script defer>
461			const messages = [
462				"This update was announced to screen readers!",
463				"Dynamic content updates work with aria-live regions.",
464				"Live regions are essential for accessible web apps.",
465				"Try this with a screen reader like NVDA or JAWS!"
466			];
467			let nextMessage = 0;
468			const announceBtn = document.getElementById('announce');
469			const contactForm = document.getElementById('contact-form');
470			const emailInput = document.getElementById('email');
471			const formStatus = document.getElementById('form-status');
472	
473			if (announceBtn) {
474				announceBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
475					document.getElementById('live-message').textContent = messages[nextMessage];
476					nextMessage = (nextMessage + 1) % messages.length;
477				});
478			}
479	
480			if (contactForm) {
481				emailInput.addEventListener('blur', () => {
482					if (emailInput.value && !emailInput.checkValidity()) {
483						emailInput.setAttribute('aria-invalid', 'true');
484						emailInput.setAttribute('aria-describedby', 'email-error');
485					} else {
486						emailInput.removeAttribute('aria-invalid');
487						emailInput.removeAttribute('aria-describedby');
488					}
489				});
490	
491				contactForm.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
492					event.preventDefault();
493					if (!contactForm.checkValidity()) {
494						formStatus.textContent = '';
495						formStatus.setAttribute('role', 'alert');
496						setTimeout(() => {
497							formStatus.textContent = 'Please fill in all required fields correctly.';
498						}, 100);
499						return;
500					}
501					formStatus.textContent = '';
502					formStatus.setAttribute('role', 'status');
503					setTimeout(() => {
504						formStatus.textContent = "Thanks! This is a demo, so nothing was sent.";
505					}, 100);
506				});
507			}
508		</script>
509	</body>
510	</html>
